Z||000000||BurlyGoat||09-27-2001||01:29 PM||||I searched for oil pressure issues and found that most people complained of oil gauge jumping all over and stuff like that....Here's my issue: when I'm sitting at a light the oil pressure starts to lower (normal), when the oil pressure gets to a certain point (not really near the red) the check engine light comes on. As soon as I accelerate the light goes off...as the pressure increases.. Computer does not throw any codes...86 V6 se<P>Any suggestions ?<P>P.S. I have a small vacuum leak (that I will find someday) so the idle is slightly high (i.e. 1500, ok more than slightly)..<P>Thanks..||||reg||1
Z||000001||falconhulk||09-27-2001||01:35 PM||||I had exactly the same problem.  My car would stall at the light after the check engine light came on unless i gave it gas. It seemed to only do this after it rained.   I disconnected the EGR valve and it did not do this for a long time.  Then one day after it rained recently the light came on but the engine did not stall.  I feel this is probably due to me removing the vacum line from the EGR and plugging it.  I am not sure what casues the check engine light as I have not been able to catch the code yet.  When I check it afterwards its always just normal 12's.  My oil pressure guage reads about 80 all the time but drops to 40 when the check engine light comes on.  BTW I have a 85 SE V6.<p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 09-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||09-27-2001||01:44 PM||||I think I would check the oil press with a good mechanical gage, finding out what it actually  is at idle,(hot and cold), and thru the acceleration range. If you are already running a 'little' high at  idle and you still have to accelerate to kick off the chk eng light, I would be more than a little concerned. It may be just a sensor or switch problem, or signs of impending bearing/oil pump failure.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BurlyGoat||09-27-2001||01:55 PM||||Amazing....my problem to a T but a different car.....I love these Fiero's.. I just got the car on the road 3 days ago and funny it rained for the last 2 days and that is the only time it happened (I drove it this morning and got stuck in some real bad traffic and it didn't do it). Odd are my EGR tube is causing the vaccuum leak, therefore is it possible that the EGR system may also cause this ?<P><BR>Thanks Again||||reg||1
Z||000004||falconhulk||09-27-2001||02:52 PM||||Another member her, Desty1, emailed me saying he was having the same problem after rain.  Its so hard to troubleshoot.  Like I said I am not sure that the EGR was the casue becasue it happened again except it did not die.  The EGR is known to stall a car on decellaration becasue its not suppose to be open on idle as it will choke the engine.  if it sticks it will stall.  You can check this.  I still want to replace my Cat with a straight pipe to the muffler but have not had the chance.  I think this also might be involved.  Since this only happens after rain and I keep it in a garage now it has not happend but 1 time in the last month after I left it out one night when it rained.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||falconhulk||10-01-2001||08:38 AM||||Had my car into the dealer the end of last week and he still cannot find the casue of this.  He wants me to leave it till it rains so he can check it out.  Here is a question for you though.....check your battery area, is it rusted at all?  What I mean it s the tray area rusted?  Is your battery loose becasue of this?||||reg||1
Z||000006||BurlyGoat||10-01-2001||12:15 PM||||Rust in the area under the vent..Of course ! It's a Fiero..Also I live in Canada.<P>Yeah, lots of rust, but I don't think the battery moves a heck of alot because I have temporarily secured it..<P>Also my car has never stalled when this happens. I really have to fix the vacuum leak as it tends to make troubleshooting other engine problems a little harder.<P>Thanks for the replies.||||reg||1
Z||000007||falconhulk||10-01-2001||12:54 PM||||My tray is rusted but I have been getting emails on this from a lot of other people with the same problem!  Probably 5 emails in the last 1 1/2 months. A couple of the guys said thier tray was rusted and one guy said he could hear his battery move when he hit the brakes!!  I have fabricated a tray support from Aluminium until I get a new tray from the dealer.  This was definitely not my problem (the battery moving) but I was thinking that a lot of water must go through there and maybe something in that area is what is getting wet.    I am just trying to track down similarities that may make troubleshooting easier.  ||||reg||1
